.\" Disable hyphenation and justification (groff man resets them per paragraph)
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.TH MKPROJ 1 "2026-10-10" "mkproj" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkproj \- small project scaffolding helper (templates, hooks, dependency metadata)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkproj create
.I name
.IR template [: variant ]
.RB [ \-\-auto\-install ]
.RB [ \-\-git ]
.RB [ \-\-code | \-C ]
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-update ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR args ...]
.br
.B mkproj add\-template
.IR source\-folder | \-
.I template\-name
.RB [ \-\-script
.IR script ]
.RB [ \-\-dependencies
.IR k=v[,k2=v2...] ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B mkproj remove\-template
.I template\-name
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B mkproj update\-dependancies
.I template\-name
.I k=v[,k2=v2...]
.br
.B mkproj list\-templates
.br
.B mkproj update\-templates
.br
.B mkproj update
.br
.B mkproj uninstall
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.br
.B mkproj completions
.BR zsh | fish
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkproj
scaffolds projects from templates.
A template is a directory of files, a config module with hook functions, or both.
Templates live in
.I ~/.config/mkproj/templates/
and config modules in
.IR ~/.config/mkproj/config/ ;
copies bundled next to the script are used as fallbacks.
Template and module names are matched case-insensitively.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create
Scaffold
.I name
from
.IR template .
Template files are copied into the project directory with
.B {{PROJECT_NAME}}
replaced, then the template's create hook runs.
.RS
.TP
.IB template : variant
Pass
.I variant
to the hook.
For bun-based templates, any variant that is not built in runs
.BI "bun create " variant\fR,
so
.B bun:astro
or
.B web:vite
work without configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-install
Install the template's missing dependencies with the system package manager.
.TP
.B \-\-git
Run
.B git init
in the new project.
.TP
.BR \-\-code ", " \-C
Open the project in VS Code.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " path"
Create the project in
.I path
instead of the current directory.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Allow an existing project: re-copy template files and run the update hook instead of the create hook.
.TP
.BI \-\- " args..."
Forward the remaining arguments to the template's tool
.RB ( "uv init" ", " "bun create" ", " "flutter create" ", ...)."
.RE
.TP
.B add\-template
Copy a folder into the user templates directory, or create a script-only template with
.BR \- .
.B \-\-script
installs a
.I create.sh
hook,
.B \-\-dependencies
writes a dependency mapping module, and
.B \-\-force
overwrites without prompting.
.TP
.B remove\-template
Remove a user template and its config module.
.TP
.B update\-dependancies
Write a legacy
.I <TEMPLATE>.conf
dependency mapping.
.TP
.B list\-templates
List user, bundled, and config-only templates.
.TP
.B update\-templates
Reinstall templates from
.B MKPROJ_TEMPLATES_REPO
(or the default repository) and the bundled copy, overwriting user templates of the same name.
.TP
.B update
Update mkproj by re-running the installer.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the mkproj binary, its PATH and completion lines, completions, and man and tldr pages.
Asks before removing
.IR ~/.config/mkproj ;
.B \-\-yes
skips all prompts.
.TP
.B completions
Print the zsh or fish completion script.
.SH BUNDLED TEMPLATES
.TP
.B C
CMake project.
.TP
.B Arduino
Arduino sketch.
.TP
.B Rust
.BR "cargo new" ;
the variant is a flag, e.g.
.BR rust:lib .
.TP
.B Python
.BR "uv init" ;
the variant is a flag, e.g.
.BR python:lib ", " python:package .
.TP
.B Go
.BR "go mod init" ,
.IR main.go ,
then
.BR "go generate" ;
the variant is the module path, e.g.
.BR go:github.com/you/app .
.TP
.B Flutter
.BR "flutter create" ;
the variant is the template, e.g.
.BR flutter:package .
.TP
.BR TypeScript ", " JavaScript
.B bun init
(JavaScript is converted from the TypeScript output).
.TP
.B Web
.BR "bun create astro" ;
variants
.BR web:react ", " web:tailwind ", " web:shadcn
.RB ( "bun init \-\-react" ),
or any
.B bun create
template.
.TP
.B Bun
.BR "bun init" ;
variants
.BR js ", " react ", " react=tailwind ", " react=shadcn ,
or any
.B bun create
template.
.SH CONFIG MODULES
A module
.I ~/.config/mkproj/config/<Template>.sh
is sourced into mkproj and may define
.BI DEPS_ TEMPLATE
(an associative array mapping commands to package names),
.BI mkproj_create_ template\fR,
and
.BI mkproj_update_ template\fR.
Hooks run from the project's parent directory and receive the project name,
project directory, variant, and any arguments given after
.BR \-\- .
Without a hook function,
.I create.sh
or
.I update.sh
in the project is run instead.
Modules are executable code; only install trusted ones.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MKPROJ_TEMPLATES_REPO
Git repository used by
.BR update\-templates .
.TP
.B MKPROJ_SHELL_SETUP
.B auto
or
.B manual
skips the installer's shell-setup prompt.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkproj/templates/
User templates.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkproj/config/
Config modules.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkproj/completions/_mkproj
zsh completion script.
.TP
.I ~/.config/fish/completions/mkproj.fish
fish completion script.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B mkproj create hello C
Create a C project in
.IR ./hello .
.TP
.B mkproj create mylib rust:lib \-\-git
Create a Rust library and initialize git.
.TP
.B mkproj create site web \-\- \-\-template minimal \-\-yes
Create an Astro site without prompts.
.TP
.B mkproj create api python \-\- \-\-python 3.12
Create a Python app with uv, pinned to Python 3.12.
.TP
.B mkproj add\-template \- myscript \-\-script ./create.sh
Add a script-only template.
